//// Front 12 step 4.3 — `@panic` aborts the program: what was printed before it
//// stays printed, nothing after it runs, and the status is non-zero. The cell
//// asserts stdout **and** the abort (`panic_aborts.exit` says `nonzero`); the
//// number itself is the runtime's (node 1, erl 1, wasmtime 134) and is not
//// pinned — see AGENTS.md § Never pin an erlang exit status.
////
//// Measured at `85f883bd` (2026-09-20): `before` then an abort on commonJS,
//// erlang, wasm and beam. The message goes to stderr on every backend, which is
//// why the cell does not read it.

pub fn main() {
    @print("before");
    @panic("boom");
    @print("after");
}
